{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/974677-help-classify-my-characters-please","id":974677,"title":"Help classify my characters, please! :)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-22T14:41:02-07:00","id":974677,"title":"Help classify my characters, please! :)","content":"Hi. Very new to Beast - I bought it yesterday. I've yet to really read the rules in depth but actually I like to come up with my character concepts first and fit them into the rules later. I feel that frees me up for more imaginative characters before I get to settled into the assumptions and stereotypes of the various splats.<br /> <br /> I've come up with a few character concepts that will be used as either pre-gens or NPCs. I'd love some advice on what Family and Hunger each should be.<br /> <br /> #1<br /> I want this character to represent the fear of a society that controls you. The cameras on every street corner, the intelligence agencies monitoring your web searches, the secret addition to the no-fly list that you have no control over and don't even know you're on. This is Kafka, Phillip K. Dick and the NWO. The character themself is going to justify (not necessarily wrongly) their creating fear and distrust in people of this kind because they think society needs more of it. They want to wise people up to how much their lives are guided and the degree to which they are spied on.<br /> <br /> #2<br /> Madness is frightening. I want a character that stokes the fear of insanity, mental illness and panic. If anyone has ever been caught up in an honest-to-god mob (I hope you haven't, I'm not talking rock concerts here), then that feeling, or when you find yourself sitting in a room full of genuine religious or political fanatics, or feel that you're losing your mind yourself. Basically that horrible feeling when you see that reality is out of reach for yourself or people around you. That can be very frightening.<br /> <br /> #3<br /> Fear of poverty / starvation / not having enough. This is very frightening to me even years after the time when I was homeless and living hand to mouth. To this day, I feel this incredible sense of relief, almost elation, every time I pay a bill or clear my credit card balance. I'm envisiaging a character that feeds on this fear in people. I think perhaps they work as a bailiff or a realtor or something. In fact, a mental image of some neatly dressed woman from the bank with a clipboard visiting a couple in their home to discuss re-mortgaging has just popped into my head fully formed.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions as to how these would be built in Beast, and even suggestions as to their monster form, would be great. I'm slowly getting my head around the game but it's 358 pages and it's taking a while. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for any replies!<br /> <br /> K.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:55:59-07:00","id":975014,"title":"","content":"#1 is definitely an Ugallu and probably a Tyrant, from my point of view. <br /> <br /> #2 strikes me as Namtaru and, depending on whether he's a stalker-type or simply unnerving, would probably be a Predator or Tyrant, respectively, although he could steal things from those he unnerves and be a Collector, I guess.<br /> <br /> #3 is almost certainly a Namtaru Tyrant, confronting people with things they don't want (poverty, destitution and lack) and shows them that it would be as easy as making a few notes on her clipboard to make those things a reality.<br /> <br /> Those are just my opinions though. feel free to agree, disagree, whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:25:07-07:00","id":975422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/974677-help-classify-my-characters-please?p=975014#post975014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#1 is definitely an Ugallu and probably a Tyrant, from my point of view.<br /> <br /> #2 strikes me as Namtaru and, depending on whether he's a stalker-type or simply unnerving, would probably be a Predator or Tyrant, respectively, although he could steal things from those he unnerves and be a Collector, I guess.<br /> <br /> #3 is almost certainly a Namtaru Tyrant, confronting people with things they don't want (poverty, destitution and lack) and shows them that it would be as easy as making a few notes on her clipboard to make those things a reality.<br /> <br /> Those are just my opinions though. feel free to agree, disagree, whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for those. I had figured #1 was probably an Ugallu but I wasn't sure about their Hunger. #2 makes sense now that I realize Namtaru don't need to be a physical revulsion per se. Madness / senility / disease all can fall under this, right? I think for what I have in mind Predator makes the most sense. I don't want the victims to feel the beast has power over them so much as a feeling of got to get away. Which indicates Predator to me.<br /> <br /> For #3, now that I understand Namtaru better, I think you're correct - that's her family. I'm struggling with her Hunger a little. I think the difficulty is that whilst I can separate a Family from who someone is psychologically, i.e. Joe feeds from people's revulsion but it doesn't define who he is or what his motivations are. However, if I make Sally a Tyrant, she's defined as someone who wants power over others.And I want to make my characters good people. So I'm struggling to pick out what suits them for Hungers. I can make it work for Vampires because the hunger for blood is a physical need. Whereas being the sort of person who wants to lord it over others is a psychological trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:40:14-07:00","id":975426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/974677-help-classify-my-characters-please?p=975422#post975422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for those. I had figured #1 was probably an Ugallu but I wasn't sure about their Hunger. #2 makes sense now that I realize Namtaru don't need to be a physical revulsion per se. Madness / senility / disease all can fall under this, right? I think for what I have in mind Predator makes the most sense. I don't want the victims to feel the beast has power over them so much as a feeling of got to get away. Which indicates Predator to me.<br /> <br /> For #3, now that I understand Namtaru better, I think you're correct - that's her family. I'm struggling with her Hunger a little. I think the difficulty is that whilst I can separate a Family from who someone is psychologically, i.e. Joe feeds from people's revulsion but it doesn't define who he is or what his motivations are. However, if I make Sally a Tyrant, she's defined as someone who wants power over others.And I want to make my characters good people. So I'm struggling to pick out what suits them for Hungers. I can make it work for Vampires because the hunger for blood is a physical need. Whereas being the sort of person who wants to lord it over others is a psychological trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't have to mean it's a physiological trait that they want, though. Someone can have - forgive me for the example - sadistic fantasies as a result of the chemical makeup of their brain or possibly a psychological disorder but that could arguably make them a better person if they choose not to act on those base desires than a person who doesn't have them in the first place. That's the crux of the matter, the difference between the Horror and the Beast. The Horror is I'd-driven, to use phychological terminology. It wants, and so it acts upon its wants. The Beast is more than that. They've got the moral super-ego in there as well, restricting their Id, represented by the Horror, from doing what it wants. Certain concessions have to be made to it but that's the job of the Ego, the mediator between the primal wants of the Id and the perfectly moral but ultimately unreasonable desires of the super-ego. It's the realist, the one in the middle. <br /> <br /> And frankly, if you want to play a character who is fully and truly 'good', even in the depths of their own mind, Beast may be the wrong game. There's a it in one of the stories in the fiction anthology where a Beast who's spent a lot of time around a Throng og prometheans is dying and as she does so, she says something like &quot;You know, I always liked the way that you thought that I was just a human with a monster attached. I could never bring myself to tell you that that was a lie.&quot; To one of them. And considering that this Beast literally fed off of destroying deceptions, that's quite a big thing.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I sort of rambled on for a while there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:45:02-07:00","id":975427,"title":"","content":"And for the Namtaru, they're the embodiment of what people don't want to face. Old age, madness, senility, harsh truths, the fact that yes, their boyfriend really is abusive, they all fall under the Namtaru. They're quite a versatile Family. A while back I made a Namtaru character whose Horror was basically a sentient void and whose lair was a solar system where the sun had burnt out, leaving only frozen planets, asteroids and the nuclear-powered complex where humans could survive. He was the representation of ending, the truth that every clock winds down, every fire fades and that no matter what we build in the meantime, the heat-death of the universe will make it all count for nought in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:50:16-07:00","id":975443,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking the time to write those. They both really help. I can work with these ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:51:47-07:00","id":975446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/974677-help-classify-my-characters-please?p=975443#post975443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for taking the time to write those. They both really help. I can work with these ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. I'm glad to have helped. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:18:08-07:00","id":978320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/974677-help-classify-my-characters-please#post974677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Very new to Beast - I bought it yesterday. I've yet to really read the rules in depth but actually I like to come up with my character concepts first and fit them into the rules later. I feel that frees me up for more imaginative characters before I get to settled into the assumptions and stereotypes of the various splats.<br /> <br /> I've come up with a few character concepts that will be used as either pre-gens or NPCs. I'd love some advice on what Family and Hunger each should be.<br /> <br /> #1<br /> I want this character to represent the fear of a society that controls you. The cameras on every street corner, the intelligence agencies monitoring your web searches, the secret addition to the no-fly list that you have no control over and don't even know you're on. This is Kafka, Phillip K. Dick and the NWO. The character themself is going to justify (not necessarily wrongly) their creating fear and distrust in people of this kind because they think society needs more of it. They want to wise people up to how much their lives are guided and the degree to which they are spied on.<br /> <br /> #2<br /> Madness is frightening. I want a character that stokes the fear of insanity, mental illness and panic. If anyone has ever been caught up in an honest-to-god mob (I hope you haven't, I'm not talking rock concerts here), then that feeling, or when you find yourself sitting in a room full of genuine religious or political fanatics, or feel that you're losing your mind yourself. Basically that horrible feeling when you see that reality is out of reach for yourself or people around you. That can be very frightening.<br /> <br /> #3<br /> Fear of poverty / starvation / not having enough. This is very frightening to me even years after the time when I was homeless and living hand to mouth. To this day, I feel this incredible sense of relief, almost elation, every time I pay a bill or clear my credit card balance. I'm envisiaging a character that feeds on this fear in people. I think perhaps they work as a bailiff or a realtor or something. In fact, a mental image of some neatly dressed woman from the bank with a clipboard visiting a couple in their home to discuss re-mortgaging has just popped into my head fully formed.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions as to how these would be built in Beast, and even suggestions as to their monster form, would be great. I'm slowly getting my head around the game but it's 358 pages and it's taking a while. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for any replies!<br /> <br /> K.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> #1 - I posted a character idea that was quite similar to this. He was an Anakim Tyrant. The giant part of him was represented as his shadow looming over the city both figuratively in the real world and quite literally in people's nightmares. He was the mayor of the city, keeping an ever watchful eye on all who lived beneath him and silencing those who fostered rebellion. Although I think being in charge of the whole city might be a little bit too powerful for a new character.<br /> <br /> <br /> #2 - For that, I would say your best bet is either an Eshmaki, or a Makara. The former represents the fear of destruction, if I recall, and the second represent the fear of the deep. The first one is obvious, you can focus on the aspect of paranoia and tension that results in people giving into pressure and losing control. The second one, you're going to have to get a lot more metaphorical in order to represent the depths of the Makara. Instead of a literal ocean, they could be the abyssal darkness that corrupts men's hearts, or the madness could stem from learning information they weren't prepared to deal with (not always of the occult persuasion). Once they're in the know, they find that they've dug too deep, and now they can't find their way back out!<br /> <br /> <br /> #3 - I don't know how similar it is, but I had another idea kind of like this who was a Namtaru (Collector?) that represented the disgust people felt towards the bottom class. His shtick was that he would hang around populated areas, fouling up the place with his presence until they gave him something he needed (or wanted) in order to convince him to move elsewhere. If they refused to provide 'donations' then he would continue to passively harass them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2016, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}